    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49468" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρ-ᾱθεν</span></b> , Adv.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from outside the door</i>: and generally,
				<i>from without</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ θ. εἴσοδοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					952
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. εἰκάσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					713
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐπεισιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GA</u>
					736b28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>outside the door, outside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ θ. ἡδονή</span>”
